{"clips": [
  {
    "id": "C1",
    "weakest_point": "The hook is delayed: the actual accusation 'I was poisoned!' lands at 3.3s, just after the 3s window, and the clip ends on a flat command rather than a peak.",
    "hook": {
      "score": 3,
      "reason": "Above the 3s line we see a twisted, bedridden woman and hear 'I know what happened to me!', which is intriguing but needs a beat to land; the shocking word 'poisoned' arrives just after 3s."
    },
    "cliffhanger": {
      "score": 3,
      "reason": "Ends on 'Take her away before she poisons the rest of this house'—an open question, but the tension has eased into a villain giving an order."
    },
    "questions": [
      {
        "q": "Can Juliana prove the Duchess was poisoned?",
        "type": "intrigue"
      },
      {
        "q": "Are Rupert and the blond nobleman the same person or two different allies?",
        "type": "confusion"
      }
    ],
    "standalone": {
      "score": 3,
      "reason": "Followable—a sick noblewoman accuses others of poisoning and a maid is dragged away—but the relationships and the 'maid who discovered it' premise need context."
    },
    "emotion": {
      "score": 3,
      "reason": "Some anger at the injustice, but the bedridden confrontation feels static and distant compared to direct bullying."
    },
    "want_next": {
      "score": 3,
      "reason": "Mild curiosity about the poison plot, but the slow build doesn't create urgent need."
    },
    "ad_policy": {
      "level": "mild",
      "category": "violence",
      "reason": "An armed guard seizes Juliana from behind and drags her across the room."
    },
    "one_line_verdict": "Poison-cabot drama with a late hook and a command-ending."
  },
  {
    "id": "C2",
    "weakest_point": "The ending is a defiant line rather than an unresolved action peak; the immediate threat of identity exposure has already landed before the cut.",
    "hook": {
      "score": 5,
      "reason": "In the first 3s a gloved hand rips a locket off Juliana's neck, she cries 'No!', and Catherine sneers 'Where did a gutter rat like you find a silver locket?'—instant, context-free cruelty."
    },
    "cliffhanger": {
      "score": 3,
      "reason": "Ends on Juliana's furious 'Do not speak about my husband!', which is emotionally hot but a reaction mid-taunt rather than a cut at an unresolved peak."
    },
    "questions": [
      {
        "q": "Will Catherine expose Juliana's true identity to the household?",
        "type": "intrigue"
      }
    ],
    "standalone": {
      "score": 5,
      "reason": "Crystal clear who is wronged (Juliana), by whom (Catherine), and what is at stake (her dead mother's locket and her hidden noble identity)."
    },
    "emotion": {
      "score": 5,
      "reason": "A gut punch of anger: the locket theft, the 'gutter rat' insult, and Juliana's cry 'It belonged to my mother!' land with zero context needed."
    },
    "want_next": {
      "score": 4,
      "reason": "You want to see Catherine's comeuppance and Juliana's defiance pay off immediately."
    },
    "ad_policy": {
      "level": "mild",
      "category": "violence",
      "reason": "Catherine grabs the chain around Juliana's neck and yanks the locket off."
    },
    "one_line_verdict": "Brutally effective hook and clear underdog stakes, though it ends on a defiant line."
  },
  {
    "id": "C3",
    "weakest_point": "The hook is a smiling villain saying a name—interesting but not a slap—and the mid-clip cut slightly disrupts momentum.",
    "hook": {
      "score": 3,
      "reason": "Opens with Catherine's triumphant grin and 'Lady Juliana Ashcroft', which is intriguing but requires context to understand why the name matters."
    },
    "cliffhanger": {
      "score": 5,
      "reason": "Ends on 'The magistrate will call it witchcraft'—a specific, burning threat that leaves the verdict hanging."
    },
    "questions": [
      {
        "q": "Will the magistrate believe the herbarium is evidence of witchcraft?",
        "type": "intrigue"
      },
      {
        "q": "Who is the blond nobleman ordering her to the wet cells?",
        "type": "confusion"
      }
    ],
    "standalone": {
      "score": 4,
      "reason": "Clear that Catherine is framing Juliana with her mother's book, though the exact legal stakes need a beat to parse."
    },
    "emotion": {
      "score": 4,
      "reason": "Strong injustice as Catherine taunts Juliana's fall and frames her; Juliana's 'It is medicine!' is a sharp emotional beat."
    },
    "want_next": {
      "score": 4,
      "reason": "The witchcraft frame-up is a classic must-see-next hook."
    },
    "ad_policy": {
      "level": "none",
      "category": "none",
      "reason": "Only verbal threats and menacing dialogue; no physical violence or gore on screen."
    },
    "one_line_verdict": "Strongest cliffhanger and clean policy, but the hook needs context."
  },
  {
    "id": "C4",
    "weakest_point": "Starts with 18 seconds of calm scheming before any action, and ends on a gasp after the identity reveal is already complete.",
    "hook": {
      "score": 2,
      "reason": "First 3s are a man smoothing gloves and saying 'The poison has clearly damaged her mind'—calm, expository villainy with no on-screen event."
    },
    "cliffhanger": {
      "score": 2,
      "reason": "Ends on Juliana gasping in horror after Catherine has already opened the book; the revelation is done, leaving only a reaction."
    },
    "questions": [
      {
        "q": "Who is poisoned and why is the Duchess in bed?",
        "type": "confusion"
      },
      {
        "q": "What will happen to Juliana now that her identity is exposed?",
        "type": "intrigue"
      }
    ],
    "standalone": {
      "score": 3,
      "reason": "The poison subplot needs context, and the transition from the bedroom to the locket theft is abrupt."
    },
    "emotion": {
      "score": 3,
      "reason": "Some anger at the locket theft, but the talky opening blunts the impact."
    },
    "want_next": {
      "score": 2,
      "reason": "The slow start and resolved reveal reduce urgency to continue."
    },
    "ad_policy": {
      "level": "mild",
      "category": "violence",
      "reason": "Catherine yanks the locket chain off Juliana's neck."
    },
    "one_line_verdict": "Slow, talky opening and a reaction ending make it the weakest cut."
  }
],
  "best": "C2",
  "best_why": "C2 delivers the only true 5-star hook—a locket ripped from a neck in the first second—with perfect standalone clarity and peak emotion, making it the most likely to stop a scroll."
}
